eck whether you need a police appointment", "for": "Everyone", "when": "Before the family travels, if possible", "need": "Passport, the letter from UDI", "why": "The family usually has to go to the police to get a residence card. The card shows that they are allowed to live in Norway.", "desc": "The letter from UDI tells you whether you need to book an appointment yourselves, and who has to attend. If you need to book, do it early – you may have to wait for an available appointment.", "call": "", "link": "https://www.politiet.no/tjenester/pass-og-id/id-for-utlendinger/"}, {"type": "first", "title": "Make sure the family has somewhere to live", "for": "Everyone", "when": "Before the family arrives", "need": "Rental agreement or other proof of housing", "why": "Without an address it is hard to get registered, get a GP, and apply for school or kindergarten.", "desc": "Make sure the home is big enough for everyone. Put everyone's names on the letterbox – important letters come by post.", "call": "", "link": ""}, {"type": "first", "title": "Collect important documents", "for": "Everyone", "when": "Before the family packs", "need": "Passports, the letter from UDI, birth certificates, vaccination records, school papers, prescriptions", "why": "Documents can be difficult to get hold of later.", "desc": "Bring originals where possible. Photograph all documents and store the images safely – for example in cloud storage.", "call": "", "link": ""}, {"type": "smart", "title": "Apply early for a kindergarten place (barnehage)", "for": "Children aged 1–5", "when": "Now", "need": "Child's date of birth and home address", "why": "Kindergarten places are allocated according to fixed application deadlines. Check the municipality's deadline so you don't miss it.", "desc": "Children living in Tønsberg may be entitled to a kindergarten place. Ask the municipality what applies to you.", "call": "", "link": "https://www.tonsberg.kommune.no/barnehage"}], [{"type": "first", "title": "Attend 